    37	- Assembled twice from a clean worktree of `270ca49`; the outputs were byte-identical.
    38	- `assemble.py --check`: agreement OK.
    39	- The installed profile matches `270ca49`'s blob.
    40	- Dry run: `prototype/e2e/driver.py` in dry mode with `--freeze-dir formal/freeze-v1`, whose freeze stage recorded
    41	  commit `270ca49` and catalog `aaf4306f…`. The verdict was `VALID_STRICT / OK`, with `utc_assessment`.
    42	- `formal/p8/vectors/check.py`: baseline and hybrid, all counts pass.
    43	
    44	The formal models were not all rerun for this record. Their results are those reviewed in E9.
    45	
    46	## The author's E9 judgments
    47	
    48	Every row has the author's decision (`docs/reviews/e9-packet/AUTHOR-RULINGS.md`, 2026-10-23). There are 27
    49	decisions over rows 1–26, because row 5 has two parts (5a, 5b):
    50	- 26 ACCEPT, at each row's bounded statement in `docs/E9-READ-PACKET.md`. This includes row 22, accepted after the
    51	  requested repairs (`docs/reviews/r22/`).
    52	- Comments and clarified scope on rows 6, 10, 13, 18 and 21. Row 23 is accepted on the corrected understanding that
    53	  the control binds temporal evidence to the exact receipt signatures committed in `A_sig`.
    54	- **Row 2 CUT:** the service-key listing (A10.4.1) is not in V1. This is the author's own narrowing of option (e),
    55	  with his rationale. It is not an invocation of the cut order.
    56	
    57	The reviewer's reservations (rows 6, 10, 18, 21) are recorded with the rulings. They stand.
    58	
    59	## What the opening permits
    60	
    61	Phase 1a opens for **V1-profile code only** (A9.2): the V1 issuer and verifier for `tessera-v1-strict`.
    62	Instrument code under `prototype/` stays instrument code. Service code may port it (owner reading,
    63	`docs/V1-FREEZE-OPEN.md`), but it must earn its own evidence on its own bytes: E10 vectors against AWS, and the P9
    64	code inspection.
    65	
    66	## What the opening does not establish
    67	
    68	- It discharges nothing in the original H0 or the full capstone gate, and no A9.3 obligation (A9.2). The capstone's
    69	  deferred questions stay open (row 18).
    70	- The models are separate results. Their composition and their preservation by an implementation are not
    71	  established (rows 10 and 21; the E8/E7/E11 sheet's gaps). The contract's guarantee table is a set of mappings,
    72	  not pairs (`docs/V1-CONTRACT.md` §5).
    73	- Instrument outputs, including the two real receipts, are not C-row evidence and discharge no obligation. They may
    74	  inform investigation and select among registered branches, as A9.2 permits.
    75	- **V1's accepted limit:** when both authority channels are captured, receipts under the captor's own keys pass.
    76	- H2 is not adjudicated.
    77	
    78	## Still to do (owner, unless marked)
    79	
    80	- **By 13 Nov:** E10 extraction.
    81	- **By 20 Nov:** the V1 issuer on AWS behind an API; the service verifier; P3's assumption half; E10 vectors run
    82	  against AWS; the P9 code inspection and its outstanding execution evidence, including the two-machine vector;
    83	  bounded local refusal; A9.4's missing-capture negative control; H3 measured.
    84	- **Before the first public verifier release** (A10.4.2):
    85	  - the custody procedure and its rehearsal;
    86	  - the production release key;
    87	  - the fingerprint channels, named by the author, independent of the operational environment by role and
    88	    credential (row 6);
    89	  - the release-format test vectors;
    90	  - the GCP VPC Service Controls perimeter;
    91	  - a policy for responses the signer was not asked for (E-06).
    92	- **4 Dec:** the relying-party test and the dead-service test. Ship or stop is the author's decision.
